Subject: raise the bytecode version for the whole patch series

What this does
  Raises the number the engine writes into compiled bytecode and checks when
  reading it back, from 27 to 28.

Why we need it
  Some of our patches change what compiled bytecode looks like. Bytecode built
  by a patched engine must not be loaded by an unpatched one, and the version
  number is how the engine refuses it -- with a clear message instead of a
  confusing failure much later.

  This is the only patch allowed to touch that number, and it applies last. If
  every patch bumped the version itself, any two of them would collide on the
  same line for reasons unrelated to what either one does, and rebasing the
  series would be a day's work instead of a minute's.

  Patches currently relying on this bump:

    0003-debugger-interface   adds an opcode
    0012-object-literal-shape-templates adds an opcode and serialized metadata
    0015-inline-caches       adds opcodes and serialized IC metadata
    0030-crc32c-bytecode-checksum changes the checksum encoding
    0031-lazy-bytecode-function-bodies changes the serialized function layout
    0038-arguments-reification-elision changes emitted argument-use opcodes
    0052-object-literal-store-fusion adds an opcode
    0064-get-loc8-array-el-fusion retires an opcode and reuses its slot
    0072-arg-key-element-load-fusion adds an opcode and reuses a retired slot
    0069-arg-field-borrow-fusion adds an opcode and reuses a retired slot
    0068-tdz-check-elimination changes emitted local-read opcodes
    0066-arg-element-and-for-in-fusion retires five opcodes and reuses their slots
    0080-compare-and-branch-fusion reuses two reserved slots for new opcodes
    0093-element-load-receiver-borrow reuses two retired slots for new opcodes
    0094-element-store-receiver-borrow reuses one reserved slot for a new opcode
    0106-escape-page-and-loc-mul adds a fused opcode and moves swap2 to the
                             escape page so OP_COUNT stays at 256
    0109-cmp-branch-fusion  adds an opcode in the banked reserved slot
    0108-i8-fusions         adds two fused opcodes and moves perm5 and rot4l to
                             the escape page so OP_COUNT stays at 256
    0107-register-vm-backend adds a serialized function tag and the register
                             bytecode blobs, which record the bumped version
    0263-regvm-global-site-cache gives the register `get_global` a cache site
                             operand
    0265-regvm-this-field-fusion adds two register opcodes
    0272-regvm-null-branches  adds four register opcodes
    0273-regvm-post-inc-fusion adds two register opcodes

  A patch that needs the version raised says so in its own header and in its
  row of README.md, and changes nothing itself.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  This is the bump.

Notes
  Three precompiled builtins ship as bytecode inside the engine, and each one
  records the version in its first byte. Raising the version without rebuilding
  them makes the engine reject its own builtins at startup: Array.fromAsync,
  Iterator.zip and Iterator.zipKeyed all fail with "invalid version". So this
  patch rebuilds them with the final patched compiler so their opcode tables and
  serialized metadata match the engine that loads them.

